    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0542" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.516/182: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-10T19:00:00-05:00">June 10, 1932—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>73. Department’s telegram No. 28.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d484-f1"/> In general
                    American business with one exception has not kept large foreign currency
                    balances in Chile. An approximate estimate of the value of these deposits is
                    $800,000 United States currency of which about $600,000 belongs to the Dupont
                    subsidiary.</p>
                <pb facs="0543" n="439" xml:id="pg439"/>
                <p>In my informal written communication to the <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi>
                    authorities yesterday I referred to a former note addressed to the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs of the Montero government in which I incorporated the policy in
                    your telegram No. 24, May 28, 2 p.m.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d484-f2"/> I said that
                    this policy applies not only to oil property but to all American property in
                    Chile. I then called attention to the adverse effect which the decree quoted in
                    my telegram No. 70, June 9, 4 p.m., would have on deposits in foreign currency
                    by Americans and on the obligation of American banks arising from their
                    trusteeship to all foreign currency depositors.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
